; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Ring of Shapes
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     rotation, penup, polygon, circle placement
; SUMMARY:  Places hexagons, triangles and stars evenly round circles to make a ring pattern like a necklace.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Instead of spinning a shape on the spot, the turtle walks out
;   from the middle without drawing, draws a shape there, walks back,
;   and turns. Three rings appear: big hexagons on the outside,
;   triangles in the middle ring, and small stars near the center.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the numbers in the three RING lines at the
;   bottom: how many shapes, how far out, and which shape.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * PENUP to move without drawing
;   * go out, draw, come back: the turtle ends where it began
;   * passing the NAME of a procedure as an input and running it with RUN
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Put 24 hexagons in the outer ring. Do they overlap?
;   * Add a fourth ring of squares.
;   * Make the shapes in a ring change color one by one.
; ============================================================

to hexagon
  repeat 6 [forward 40 right 60]
end

to triangle
  repeat 3 [forward 45 right 120]
end

to star
  repeat 5 [forward 30 right 144]
end

; :count copies of a shape, each :distance from the middle.
; :shape is a word like "hexagon. RUN (list :shape) runs it.
to ring :count :distance :shape :color
  setpencolor :color
  repeat :count [
    penup forward :distance pendown
    run (list :shape)
    penup back :distance pendown
    right 360 / :count
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [255 250 240]
setpensize 3
ring 16 210 "hexagon [40 120 200]
ring 12 130 "triangle [220 80 60]
ring 8 55 "star [230 160 20]
